#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073753 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073446 :question/id #uuid "707504e8-a367-5dc2-a663-371a9dcf7224" :question/math-academy-id "e-13010" :question/problem "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n${2u + 9v - 6 = 0; 2u + 6v - 8 = 0$" :question/worked-solution "Sometimes, it's handy to assign a number to each equation in a system, so that we can refer to them more easily:\n\n$$\n{2u + 9v - 6 = 0(1); 2u + 6v - 8 = 0(2)\n$$\n\nWe will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. Using equation $\\color{blue}(2)$, we can solve for $u$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 2u+6v-8 &= 0 \\\\ 2u+6v &= 8 \\\\ 2u &= 8 - 6v \\\\ u &= \\dfrac{8-6v}{2} \\\\ u &= 4 - 3v \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $u=4-3v$ into equation $\\color{red}(1)$ and solve for $v$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 2u+9v-6 &= 0 \\\\ 2(4-3v)+9v-6 &= 0 \\\\ 8-6v+9v-6 &= 0 \\\\ 2+3v &= 0 \\\\ 3v &= -2 \\\\ v &= -\\dfrac{2}{3} \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute\n\n$$\nv=-\\dfrac{2}{3}\n$$\n\ninto equation $\\color{red}(1)$, then we can find the value of $u$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 2u+9v-6 &= 0 \\\\ 2u+9\\left(-\\dfrac{2}{3}\\right) -6 &= 0 \\\\ 2u-6-6 &= 0 \\\\ 2u-12 &= 0 \\\\ 2u &= 12 \\\\ u &= 6 \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $u=6$ and\n\n$$\nv=-\\dfrac{2}{3}\n$$\n\n, which can be written as\n\n$$\n\\left(6,-\\dfrac{2}{3}\\right)\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4352698-7af7-5d74-9c3a-0f951c3e6078" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073997 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a72bb5e1-600c-5bc3-9a20-8a9139d96608" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p = 4, q = 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186070068} {:answer/id #uuid "db48f86d-2fc7-507b-bdea-a2a005a0b680" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p = 4, q =-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186070069} {:answer/id #uuid "02252a99-76f0-5313-9df0-f9ec9acc8c20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p = 4, q = 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186070070} {:answer/id #uuid "3b9ad275-7db8-59c8-8912-f40f971d2f8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p = 3, q = 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186070071} {:answer/id #uuid "6285edaa-20b3-59cd-9749-0f49e5e95580" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p =-4, q = 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186070072}] :answer-field/id #uuid "76642104-cdd8-5320-bbe7-97e833212d5e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186070067}] :question/id #uuid "833a2ed3-b37f-5ade-bd6a-5fdaf64b6506" :question/math-academy-id "q-12444" :question/problem "Using the method of substitution, find the solution of\n${-3p + q =-9; 5p + 4q = 32$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073998 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "840a66d8-a769-5b7d-9b3e-56e75696fb72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a =-4, b = 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186070074} {:answer/id #uuid "885a205a-2ea2-543d-94ad-dd8f41804a39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a = 3, b =-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186070075} {:answer/id #uuid "8b98aa0f-2e3d-5c66-a1e2-83fb7ee036b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a = 4, b =-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186070076} {:answer/id #uuid "b1e7e93a-adf5-514b-a6ad-8218c526bbc3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a = 2, b =-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186070077} {:answer/id #uuid "1cacef46-ef5e-5b1b-814c-14b3f44ea4fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a =-2, b = 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186070078}] :answer-field/id #uuid "3f914bec-7e6e-58f8-a49c-484a6a89ef3a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186070073}] :question/id #uuid "90bf8b55-699c-5e18-b484-90473cb6a72f" :question/math-academy-id "q-12457" :question/problem "Using the method of substitution, find the solution of\n\n${-7a + 2b = 18; -6a + 6b = 0$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186074047 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "108d90bc-6b5c-5888-a441-c0910faf7b57" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186070290} {:answer/id #uuid "3afa1d5f-dfe6-59bc-8683-638f0716320d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "26" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186070291} {:answer/id #uuid "5b963b53-bada-5f5f-9e14-bb49282b0719" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186070292} {:answer/id #uuid "637fb8f3-b4ed-5b3b-b5dc-ae08c01f9ce3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186070293} {:answer/id #uuid "71ce6b5e-047a-5e92-8750-073b719123cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186070294}] :answer-field/id #uuid "8b1211a7-7190-520c-ac4c-581ede5f3f0f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186070289}] :question/id #uuid "a7c18dc6-0363-5db7-9c51-22de1db359fc" :question/math-academy-id "q-18483" :question/problem "Given the system of equations below, what is the value of $p - q$?\n\n${5q + 55 = 0; 2p + 3q + 3 = 0$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Challenging System of Linear Equations Using Substitution"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073776 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073480 :question/id #uuid "f2105fec-c85b-5928-92e6-95ed80f1326c" :question/math-academy-id "e-14009" :question/problem "Show that the following system of equations has no solution.\n\n${4x + 2y = 4; 2x + y = 4$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by solving the system using elimination.\n\nNotice that if we multiply the second equation by $-2$, then we will get a $-4x$ term that can cancel with the $4x$ term in the first equation:\n\n$$\n{4x + 2y = 4; 2x + y = 4 \\mid \\mid \\cdot (-2)\n$$\n\nWhen we add the two equations, it turns out that both variables cancel, and we obtain a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n4x + 2y &= 4 \\\\\n- 4x - 2y &= -8 \\\\\n0 &= (4 - 8) \\\\\n0 &= -4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe statement $0=-4$ is *always false*. Therefore, we conclude that the system has *no solutions*.\n\nGeometrically, this means that the corresponding lines *do not intersect*. In other words, they are *parallel.*\n\n![](images/04/048c377f99093f493c37bc4de0363527996c8928348b43ad9c9747965f984c1f.png)"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a24fb4f3-6e3c-5c45-b31e-85b7ce290eda" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049310 :topic/math-academy-id 1414 :topic/title "Linear Equations With Infinitely Many Solutions"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050190 :topic/math-academy-id 4026 :topic/title "Solving Systems of Linear Equations Using Elimination: One Transformation"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186074059 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a18f1824-3dc6-5be0-ac2f-8dc7d149ea49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "no solutions" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186070311} {:answer/id #uuid "c2a5f92e-26c3-577c-9607-de562db7346c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "infinitely many solutions" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186070312} {:answer/id #uuid "64558df4-ad83-5b34-a3b7-63fff9c0d7aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a single solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186070313}] :answer-field/id #uuid "f25dca02-f19e-5b90-85b6-f363b7822cfc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186070310}] :question/id #uuid "db4ced0c-7aa1-5612-b60c-da9238f3ca28" :question/math-academy-id "q-211984" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n\n${6x + 4y = 6; - 2x - y = 5$\n\nThis system of equations has {{field-1}}."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186074086 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e68ea0f6-0c4b-5948-83f5-ff28c2e4168d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a single solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186070367} {:answer/id #uuid "2538c1b9-bfe4-5a49-9a4d-041fb3280dc6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "infinitely many solutions" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186070368} {:answer/id #uuid "3052b8bd-d15e-5191-af99-65807ded222d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "no solutions" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186070369}] :answer-field/id #uuid "56f7931c-2301-53d0-aff9-d64e1ec4c799" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186070366}] :question/id #uuid "cc576833-ebf9-5c8f-b749-c0cfe585139d" :question/math-academy-id "q-237043" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n\n${y - 3x - 2 = 0; 4y - 12x - 8 = 0$\n\nThis system of equations has {{field-1}}."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186074087 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a63e30c0-cda9-58f0-aaa0-0b5e17e4d7b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "no solutions" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186070371} {:answer/id #uuid "ebda1ec7-dc47-5ae4-88f3-b0e4338d63a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "infinitely many solutions" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186070372} {:answer/id #uuid "f7cb9713-fa2b-59a2-b51d-c8360c95fceb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a single solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186070373}] :answer-field/id #uuid "59fc212c-55f0-5857-8850-50ee3e15dd2f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186070370}] :question/id #uuid "a43ef3b0-9627-5633-9a33-9830700deff8" :question/math-academy-id "q-237046" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n\n${2x - 5y = 15; 4x - 10y =-10$\n\nThis system of equations has {{field-1}}."}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Number of Solutions to a System"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073777 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073481 :question/id #uuid "b1d34db3-7f30-5a8c-b233-fd955ac656f0" :question/math-academy-id "e-14011" :question/problem "At how many points do the lines $x - 2y = 2$ and $10y - 5x = -10$ intersect?" :question/worked-solution "The number of points of intersection between the two lines is equal to the number of solutions of the corresponding system:\n\n$$\n{x - 2y = 2; 10y - 5x =-10\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using substitution. First, we solve for $x$ in the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx - 2y &= 2 \\\\\nx &= 2y + 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute\n\n$$\nx=2y+2\n$$\n\ninto the second equation and solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n10y - 5x &= -10 \\\\\n10y - 5(2y + 2) &= -10 \\\\\n10y - 10y - 10 &= -10 \\\\\n- 10 &= -10\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe result is a statement that's always true. Therefore, we conclude that the system has infinitely many solutions.\n\nConsequently, the lines intersect at infinitely many points (i.e., they coincide)."} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5fab4792-0fe1-5a5c-8754-509af469da68" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049869 :topic/math-academy-id 408 :topic/title "Calculating the Intersection of Two Lines"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050245 :topic/math-academy-id 837 :topic/title "Parallel Lines in the Coordinate Plane"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186074060 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b4213192-05bd-5441-ab8f-5601edb4f46a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at infinitely many points" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186070315} {:answer/id #uuid "d06783b6-d3ed-5f45-826b-a57ede5f7c52" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at one point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186070316} {:answer/id #uuid "3a739d2b-bb1e-5a44-b0f7-82240d439868" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "do not intersect" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186070317}] :answer-field/id #uuid "2054f218-d7fb-5f4b-bb1e-7462237fd4e8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186070314}] :question/id #uuid "dffc4e2c-f9ea-5274-92e6-4d3948a4c014" :question/math-academy-id "q-211986" :question/problem "Consider the lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$, defined as\n$l_{1}: 2x - y =-2, l_{2}: 6x - 3y =-12$.\n\nAt how many points do these lines intersect?\n\nThe lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$ {{field-1}}."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186074089 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b83e75eb-68ab-567d-a460-9470152445c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at one point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186070381} {:answer/id #uuid "fb057ae1-6d19-5e10-9555-8ef14e34ac05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "do not intersect" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186070382} {:answer/id #uuid "6a6737ed-0efb-5044-904e-0bbf76ec3016" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at infinitely many points" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186070383}] :answer-field/id #uuid "19065220-42bb-5118-b439-9be235fa2f10" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186070380}] :question/id #uuid "c2c1547a-6290-54a8-97be-3db72633dabf" :question/math-academy-id "q-237095" :question/problem "Consider the lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$, defined as\n$l_{1}: y = 3x - 4, l_{2}: 12x - 4y = 16$.\n\nAt how many points do these lines intersect?\n\nThe lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$ {{field-1}}."}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Number of Intersection Points of Two Lines"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073778 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073482 :question/id #uuid "ab09c3eb-6813-57c6-891b-bf20196cbe93" :question/math-academy-id "e-14014" :question/problem "Find all points of intersection of the lines $3x+2y=2$ and $6x+4y=4$." :question/worked-solution "The points of intersection of the lines correspond to the solutions of the following system:\n\n$$\n{3x + 2y = 2; 6x + 4y = 4\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using elimination. Notice that if we multiply the first equation by $-2$, then we will get a $-6x$ term that can cancel with the $6x$ term in the second equation:\n\n$$\n{3x + 2y = 2 \\mid \\mid \\cdot (-2); 6x + 4y = 4\n$$\n\nWhen we add the two equations, it turns out that both variables cancel, and we obtain a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-6x - 4y &= -4 \\\\\n6x + 4y &= 4 \\\\\n0 &= (-4 + 4) \\\\\n0 &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBecause we obtained a true statement, we conclude that there are infinitely many solutions to the system. Therefore, the lines have infinitely many intersection points.\n\nWe want to find an expression that represents every solution to the system. Any value of $x$ is a solution, and we can find the corresponding $y$-coordinate for each $x$-coordinate by solving one of the lines for $y$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n3x + 2y &= 2 \\\\\n2y &= 2 - 3x \\\\\ny &= \\frac{2 - 3x}{2} \\\\\ny &= 1 - \\frac{3}{2}x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the points of intersection are\n\n$$\n\\left(x,1-\\dfrac{3}{2}x \\right)\n$$\n\nwhere $x$ is any number."} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "50351666-c691-510f-863c-168c61f9980b" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050622 :topic/math-academy-id 356 :topic/title "Solving Two-Variable Equations"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186074057 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/id #uuid "3bd07937-83d7-59ef-b1a0-dfa3f718f86f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186070308}] :question/id #uuid "10ef6686-7543-50bc-a43e-d807d37d1e95" :question/math-academy-id "q-208832" :question/problem "Describe the points that lie on the intersection of the lines $x - 4y =-3$ and $2x - 8y =-6$. Express your answer in terms of $x$ only.The intersection points are $(x$,\n{{field-1}}\n$)$, where $x$ is any number."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186074138 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ec4c6de4-a7fd-5851-accd-9c5156477afd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, 2x - 3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186071026} {:answer/id #uuid "f81e9c0d-0f7f-5808-ae52-8f03e0039400" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, x + 2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186071027} {:answer/id #uuid "0e89162b-dfe2-5744-9796-d0f1635ed693" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, 3x + 2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186071028} {:answer/id #uuid "49a90275-fbc9-561c-b080-6352f5ee175a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, x + 3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186071029} {:answer/id #uuid "677e1be5-b5d0-5254-975c-3550e4fc1853" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, 3x - 2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186071030}] :answer-field/id #uuid "4ea64686-cfe1-5de1-94d2-5c5e04adbf93" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186071025}] :question/id #uuid "cb252b96-4a13-53c2-bed5-4b7dd119cf7c" :question/math-academy-id "q-25524" :question/problem "Find all points of intersection of the lines $9x - 3y =-6$ and $3x - y =-2$."}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to a System With Infinitely Many Intersection Points"}]}
